{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-8","id":"msg_01AFfzJ5mRqKxgoGruMzXg9Y","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"**Anchor** is a personal productivity + R&D mission-control system built for J.C. Liechty, living entirely in one folder (`C:\\dev\\Anchor`), Python-stdlib-only (one declared `pywinpty` exception).\n\n- **Purpose â€” a personal GTD/task system backed by plain markdown.** Tasks, projects, inbox, and per-domain files (academic, commercial, family, writing) are the source of truth as plain `.md` files. There's no database â€” every change is written straight back to markdown and logged. Task lifecycle: Active â†’ Done / Cancelled / Saved-for-Later / Restored.\n\n- **What it ships â€” `anchor_gui.py`, a self-contained local web dashboard.** It's the one declared deliverable: a stdlib HTTP server (no framework) that regenerates the full dashboard HTML per request, exposes a `/api/*` endpoint surface, and writes directly to the markdown. It runs persistently as the NSSM Windows service `anchor` on `http://localhost:8777`. A CLI mirror (`anchor.py`) provides the same operations and generates a static `dashboard.html`.\n\n- **It has grown into a \"Project Cockpit\" for trio-driven R&D.** Beyond tasks, each project gets a per-project window that drives the research â†’ planning â†’ build trio (researchPrime Â· Crucible Â· Foreman). Each lane shows its most-recent session as a tile with one honest status light (green/amber/red/grey), and clicking expands an inline panel: a cached, grounded summary on top and a real, resizable terminal below.\n\n- **Real interactive terminals over ConPTY.** Sessions run server-side via `pywinpty`/ConPTY (the lone waiver of the stdlib-only rule), each isolated in its own git worktree+branch, streamed to xterm.js over a hand-rolled WebSocket (with SSE/POST fallback), surviving disconnect. A session's lane skill auto-loads and greets exactly once â€” no repeating-prompt loop.\n\n- **Supporting machinery, all stdlib + cached/grounded.** Durable session registry, append-only effort/cost history (tokensÂ·$Â·time rollups), validated generate-twice + grounding-filtered summaries, stage handoffs, deliverable pin/declare/launch-by-type, and ephemeral deliverable previews hard-guarded to never bind port 8777 or touch live data.\n\n- **Self-verifying.** A 5:00 AM scheduled health check parses every markdown file, exercises every endpoint on a throwaway port, and walks the fully-stubbed v2/v3/v4 R&D surfaces (no live `claude`, no real data touched), writing a daily report and surfacing failures as a red dashboard banner.\n\nThe R&D surface has shipped through **v4 \"Project Cockpit\"** (built by Foreman, merged to master 2026-06-13), with v2/v3 also merged earlier."}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":4412,"cache_creation_input_tokens":24728,"cache_read_input_tokens":20597,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":24728},"output_tokens":2,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"72ef7c4a-99b0-4743-ad50-3f417deddeda","uuid":"7926c893-5892-4ac2-8820-3a66fcb81094","request_id":"req_011Cc1fEAGMqXvMtg7hiMT8n"}
